  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Conceptualizing the Dance App**\n\nI\'m now focusing on the dance class booking app concept, inspired by the \"PLANA\" Chinese app. I\'m exploring features based on the provided screenshots, and determining the key elements for a successful dance studio app. This involves understanding user flow and essential functionalities. I\'m prioritizing user experience and ease of booking.\n\n\n**Deconstructing the PLANA App**\n\nNow I\'m diving deeper, taking apart the PLANA app\'s structure based on those screenshots. I\'ve pinpointed its key sections: the header with schedule options, category filters (Group, Private, Series), the \"Bookable Only\" toggle and date selection, and detailed course cards. I\'m focusing on dissecting each element for user-friendliness and effective booking flow. The details on each course card are providing great information.\n\n\n**Analyzing Booking Mechanics**\n\nI\'m now thoroughly examining the booking mechanics. I\'m noting the clear indications of booking availability and statuses like \"\345\267\262\347\273\223\346\235\237,\" \"\351\242\204\347\272\246,\" and \"\346\216\222\351\230\237,\" each conveyed with distinct button colors. I\'m exploring the \"05\346\234\21024\346\227\245 00:00\345\217\257\347\272\246\" message indicating future booking availability and the calendar modal. The filter drawer and weekly view is another important set of details.\n\n\n**Defining App Navigation**\n\nI\'m now identifying the core app navigation components, focusing on a tabbed bottom bar. The tabs will include: Home (`\351\246\226\351\241\265`), Schedule/Book (`\350\257\276\350\241\250`), Store (`\345\225\206\345\237\216`), and Profile (`\346\210\221\347\232\204`). I\'m aiming for a straightforward and intuitive layout, inspired by the app, that provides quick access to essential features. I\'m prioritizing user experience and navigation.\n\n\n**Designing the Responsive Layout**\n\nI\'m now focusing on designing the responsive layout with a premium studio feel. I\'m prioritizing a mobile-centric approach with a frame on desktop and full-width on mobile. I\'m focusing on the implementation of the core booking interface (`\350\257\276\350\241\250`) with both daily and weekly schedule views. I am also working on the support for toggles (group, private, series classes), and a date carousel at the top, synchronized with the custom calendar selector. I\'m incorporating a filter modal by classroom and teacher, along with text filtering. Booking actions, like clicking \"\351\242\204\347\272\246\" to book and decrement spots, and clicking \"\346\216\222\351\230\237\" to join a queue, are key interactions.\n\n\n**Refining Class Management**\n\nI\'m now detailing class booking changes: \"\345\217\226\346\266\210\351\242\204\347\272\246\" with refund controls for booked classes; a \"\345\217\257\347\272\246\" toggle for bookable classes. I\'m focusing on the \"Store\" feature for membership card purchases (simulated payment). Finally, in \"Profile\", I will include user avatar, pass balance, booking history (upcoming, completed, queue), and integrated stats (dance hours, favorite styles). I need to determine the right assets now.\n\n\n**Planning Visual Assets**\n\nI\'m now prioritizing the visual design and asset acquisition for this project. I will focus on crafting a beautiful UI using Tailwind CSS, coupled with SVGs and Lucide React icons. I will not use any non-relevant integrations like OAuth or Firebase to keep things simple. I need to update the `name` and `description` of the app in the `metadata.json` file. Next, I will inspect `metadata.json`, `package.json`, and the current folder structure to assess their contents and confirm their states, then formulate a comprehensive design plan.\n\n\n"
    modified_response: "I will begin by inspecting the existing files in the project workspace, including `metadata.json` and `package.json` to gather context about the existing dependencies and config."
    thinking_duration {
      seconds: 11
      nanos: 410436467
    }
    stop_reason: STOP_REASON_STOP_PATTERN
  }
}
