  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Designing Application Layout**\n\nI\'m now focusing on designing the application\'s layout. Initial screenshots are in Chinese, so I\'m paying attention to how the \"daily schedule,\" \"weekly schedule,\" \"group class,\" \"private lesson,\" \"class,\" \"available,\" \"filter,\" \"booked,\" \"finished,\" \"appointment,\" and \"queue\" screens will integrate.\n\n\n**Refining User Interface Design**\n\nI\'m now diving deep into user interface refinements. I\'ve decided on either standard English labels alongside bilingual display or a fully polished bilingual interface mirroring the original screenshots. I\'m building `/src/components/ScheduleView.tsx` with toggles for daily/weekly layouts, a date-sliding carousel, tabs for course types, and a \"\345\217\257\347\272\246\" limit toggle. I\'m also implementing the calendar picker modal and a drawer filter for classroom and teacher selections.\n\n\n**Implementing Course Card Details**\n\nI\'m now fully immersed in implementing the course card details. I\'m focusing on the precise time overlays, the circular avatars with modern borders, and the various status logics. I\'m carefully incorporating the \"\345\267\262\347\273\223\346\235\237\" (Ended), date-based \"\345\217\257\347\272\246\" (Available), \"\346\216\222\351\230\237\" (Queue), \"\351\242\204\347\272\246\" (Book) and \"\345\217\226\346\266\210\351\242\204\347\272\246\" (Cancel Book) states and their corresponding button functionalities. I\'m prioritizing the user experience of course availability.\n\n\n"
    modified_response: "I will now create the main booking schedule component `/src/components/ScheduleView.tsx`. This contains:\n1. **Daily View (\346\227\245\350\257\276\350\241\250)** / **Weekly View (\345\221\250\350\257\276\350\241\250)** dual interface.\n2. Category filters: Group (\345\233\242\350\257\276), Private (\347\247\201\346\225\231), and Series (\347\217\255\350\257\276) selectors.\n3. Live date-scroller carousel matching the exact layout of the screenshots.\n4. An interactive Calendar Picker dialog allowing the user to select dates as shown in the mockup image.\n5. A fully-functional slide-out Drawer Filter matching the layout of Image 8 (choose Room/Teacher, Reset, Confirm).\n6. Double-state Booking mechanism:\n   - \"\351\242\204\347\272\246\" (Book, teal state): reduces user course passes by 1, flags as booked.\n   - \"\346\216\222\351\230\237\" (Waitlist, red state): triggers waitlist queue registration.\n   - Already booked blocks support simple tap-to-refund/cancel.\n7. Color-coded Weekly Scheduler blocks reflecting images 7 and 10, with clickable details. This delivers a rich, responsive interface."
    thinking_duration {
      seconds: 4
      nanos: 579168848
    }
