  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Analyzing Style Differences**\n\nOkay, I\'m starting to dissect the styling components within `ScheduleView.tsx`. Initially, I\'ve identified the `bg-slate-50` content page container. I\'ve begun to compare this to the `bg-indigo-50/20` which will be used in the new \"Vibrant Palette\" aesthetic. I am aiming to systematically address each styling element in the component.\n\n\n**Refining Component Aesthetics**\n\nI\'m now focusing on specific styling details within `ScheduleView.tsx`. The title divider, currently `border-slate-150`, is under consideration for a bolder `border-b-4 border-yellow-400 bg-white` or simple styling. The studio icon\'s appearance is evolving from `w-5 h-5 rounded-full bg-teal-500` to a more dynamic look: `w-6 h-6 rounded-full bg-rose-500 flex items-center justify-center text-white text-xs font-black rotate-45`. Text styling is getting refinements too.\n\n\n**Enhancing Interface Elements**\n\nI\'m now concentrating on styling refinements for the type filter, transforming its look to `bg-indigo-50 border border-indigo-100 p-1 rounded-2xl flex space-x-1 shrink-0`. I\'ve also updated the `onlyBookable` switch to use a `bg-rose-500` for the active state and `bg-indigo-200` for inactive. The calendar button\'s now `border border-indigo-100 shadow-sm bg-white cursor-pointer hover:bg-rose-50 hover:text-rose-500 text-indigo-900`. I\'m refreshing date carousel styling with `bg-indigo-900 text-white shadow-md border-b-4 border-yellow-400 scale-105` when selected and a hover effect, plus updated date name labels.\n\n\n**Adjusting Visual Signifiers**\n\nI\'m now iterating on visual cues within the listings. I\'ve updated the selected date text to be `text-yellow-300`, and all other dates to `text-indigo-400 font-bold`. The filter and listings labels are now `text-rose-500 font-extrabold` on a `bg-rose-50` background. I\'ve also swapped out the filter button styling, and I\'ve started on empty stage components and class item listings visual adjustments. I am currently honing the class item styling.\n\n\n**Refining Element Styling**\n\nI\'m now integrating new styles into class item listings. For text, I\'m using `bg-yellow-400 text-indigo-900 font-black rounded-lg px-1 text-[10px]`. Capacity indicators will use `text-rose-500 font-black` when full, and otherwise `text-indigo-900 font-black`. For booking action buttons, the \"Ended\" and \"Not Open\" states use `bg-indigo-50 text-indigo-305`. I have defined styles for booked banners and various queue/waitlist actions and also an empty spot button. I also styled calendar grid and filter drawers.\n\n\n"
    thinking_duration {
      seconds: 7
      nanos: 567057137
    }
    stop_reason: STOP_REASON_STOP_PATTERN
  }
}
