,\" the default dark mode; \"Vibrant Street Light,\" a recommended clean, warm theme; \"Cool Mint & Lavender,\" with a techwear edge; and \"Brutalist Chalk,\" offering an artistic, street-art vibe. I\'m focusing on implementation in `App.tsx` and considering a global theme state or container class to manage these styles.\n\n\n**Prioritizing Light Theme**\n\nI\'m now prioritizing the new \"Vibrant Street Light\" theme. I\'ve decided to make it the default style to address the user\'s initial feedback about the darkness. Implementing this involves updating the `currentTheme` state in `App.tsx` and creating a simple selector. I\'ll focus on the specific color mapping for this theme, defining the background as warm white, and accents as a punchy rose-coral and golden-peach. This solves the immediate problem and lets me satisfy the user!\n\n\n**Defining Theme Variables**\n\nI\'m now defining the specific variables for each theme, primarily focusing on `midnight`, `mint-lavender`, and a light mode. I\'m choosing to utilize TypeScript-based style maps to manage this cleanly, including background, text, and accent colors for a simple implementation. The light mode will use a white background and soft shadows.\n\n\n"
