  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Analyzing the Component Structure**\n\nI\'m now diving into the component structure. I\'ve pinpointed `/src/components/HomeView.tsx` as a key file. But before modifying that, I\'ll tackle the WeChat Authorize View. I\'m checking `App.tsx` for layout handling, to understand the broader context.\n\n\n**Implementing Authorization Logic**\n\nI\'ve added an `isAuthorized` state to `App.tsx` and am now persisting it using `localStorage`. If the user isn\'t authorized, the app will render a dedicated WeChat Authorized Login Screen. I\'m focusing on crafting this screen\'s UI based on screenshot details. I have the status bar info, logo & Chinese characters now! I\'m planning CSS layout & graphics now.\n\n\n**Designing the Login Screen**\n\nI\'m now focusing on the visual design of the WeChat login screen. I\'m starting with the text layout, specifically the heading hierarchy and button styling. The black block tag and main title need accurate rendering. I\'m implementing the two buttons: the vivid mint/teal gradient for \"\345\276\256\344\277\241\346\216\210\346\235\203\347\231\273\345\275\225\" and the light gray \"\345\217\226\346\266\210\" button, aiming for pixel-perfect replication of their appearance. I\'ll need to figure out the best approach to the custom checkbox agreement row at the bottom.\n\n\n**Refining Screen Flow**\n\nI\'m now integrating the agreement checkbox and \"Register\" link into the WeChat login screen, exactly as shown in the screenshots! I\'m adding a toast to prompt users to agree to the terms before authorization. If they agree, the screen will transition smoothly to `HomeView`. I\'m also planning to incorporate a \"Logout\" button, probably in `ProfileView`, for returning to the login screen.\nI am now deciding on our color theme.\n\n\n**Updating the HomeView**\n\nI\'m now focusing on redesigning `HomeView.tsx` to match the second screenshot. I\'m prioritizing the bottom navigation bar and will verify the icons are correct for \"\351\246\226\351\241\265,\" \"\350\257\276\350\241\250,\" \"\345\225\206\345\237\216,\" and \"\346\210\221\347\232\204.\" I\'ve confirmed that the existing `lucide-react` icons are suitable as pristine vector SVGs. Now I\'m ready to tackle the main banner, which requires a custom slider incorporating the title \"\345\245\263\347\245\236\346\226\260\345\256\240\345\262\202\346\255\242\344\272\216\345\245\275\" and a red \"\347\253\213\345\215\263\345\274\200\346\212\242 >\" button, as well as a high-quality fitness image.\n\n\n**Crafting Carousel Slides**\n\nI\'m now crafting the content for the HomeView\'s carousel. I\'ve got the first slide design focused. It will prominently feature a fitness professional\'s pose with an eye-catching red \"\347\253\213\345\215\263\345\274\200\346\212\242 >\" button, directly leading to a purchase dialog for a yoga course package. I am designing a summer jazz boot camp slide, and a beginner street dance program slide, too. I\'m focusing on the compelling copy for each.\n\n\n\n**Adding Feature Elements**\n\nI\'m now adding features to the HomeView! I\'ve decided on icons for the navigation bar, including `Ticket` or `CalendarDays` for \'Schedule\' (\350\257\276\350\241\250), and a `Coins` icon with a gold/yellow circle for \"Points,\" which will trigger an interactive Points Exchange Modal/Drawer. This modal will have several exchange options like \"PLANA \351\231\220\351\207\217\347\211\210\350\277\220\345\212\250\346\257\233\345\267\276\" and will update the system state and show a success toast on successful exchanges! I\'m also adding a \"\345\245\275\347\211\251\346\216\250\350\215\220\" section with a \"\346\233\264\345\244\232 >\" link to the Store view.\n\n\n**Designing the Product Grid**\n\nI\'m now diving into the product grid for the HomeView. I\'m focusing on two example products. For the first, I\'m using a striking street dance image and detailed sales points, including 1-on-1 feedback. The second, a white sweatshirt, will showcase a sharp Unsplash photo with size selection. Both will trigger a purchase slide sheet upon click, so users can make a smooth purchase with the desired payment options!\n\n\n"
    modified_response: "I will view `/src/components/ProfileView.tsx` around the bottom of the component to see where I can place a polished \"\351\200\200\345\207\272\347\231\273\345\275\225\" (Logout/Switch Account) button, allowing the user to seamlessly toggle between the authorized application dashboard and the mock WeChat Authorized Login flow shown in the first screenshot."
    thinking_duration {
      seconds: 12
      nanos: 148312442
    }
    stop_reason: STOP_REASON_STOP_PATTERN
  }
